# UI — Eye Comfort (Always)

For **any** UI, HTML, CSS, docs site, preview page, or generated styles in this project, follow these defaults without asking. Do not revert to pure white/black, tiny text, or non-Inter body fonts.

## Font — Inter

- Primary: `Inter, system-ui, sans-serif`
- Load Inter (Google Fonts, fontsource, or `@font-face`)
- Do not use Roboto, Arial, or system-only stacks as the primary face

## Colors — eye comfort

Avoid pure `#FFFFFF` backgrounds and pure `#000000` text (and the reverse on dark UI). Use soft neutrals:

| Token | Light (default) | Dark (if dark UI) |
|-------|-----------------|-------------------|
| Background | `#F5F5F4` | `#1C1C1E` |
| Surface / cards | `#FAFAF9` | `#252528` |
| Text primary | `#292524` | `#E7E5E4` |
| Text muted | `#57534E` | `#A8A29E` |
| Border | `#E7E5E4` | `#3F3F46` |
| Link / accent | `#1D4ED8` | `#93C5FD` |

```css
/* ✅ GOOD */
:root {
  color-scheme: light;
  --bg: #f5f5f4;
  --text: #292524;
  --text-muted: #57534e;
  background-color: var(--bg);
  color: var(--text);
  font-family: Inter, system-ui, sans-serif;
}

/* ❌ BAD */
background: #fff;
color: #000;
font-size: 12px;
```

## Type scale — standard sizes

| Role | Size | Line height |
|------|------|-------------|
| Body | **16px** (`1rem`) | **1.6** |
| Small / secondary | 14px (`0.875rem`) | 1.5 |
| H3 | 1.25rem (20px) | 1.4 |
| H2 | 1.5rem (24px) | 1.35 |
| H1 | 1.875rem (30px) | 1.3 |
| Code | 0.875rem–1rem | 1.5 |

- Default body text is **16px** — never ship UI body at 12–13px
- Comfortable measure: ~65–75 characters per line where practical
- Font weight: 400 body, 500–600 labels/headings (not ultra-thin)

## Tailwind defaults (when used)

```js
theme: {
  extend: {
    fontFamily: { sans: ["Inter", "system-ui", "sans-serif"] },
    colors: {
      canvas: "#F5F5F4",
      ink: "#292524",
      muted: "#57534E",
    },
    fontSize: {
      base: ["1rem", { lineHeight: "1.6" }],
    },
  },
}
```

Body: `bg-canvas text-ink font-sans text-base antialiased`.

## Scope

Applies to web UI, landing pages, HTML previews, and any styled docs. Plain `.md` study notes need no CSS unless a preview/site is added — then these tokens apply.

## Never ask again

These are project defaults. Apply automatically on every UI/styling task.
